## 3. Status

### Done and verified

Foundation layer. **26/26 tests pass, `tsc --noEmit` clean.**

- `src/types.ts` — types shared across the postMessage boundary. All JSON-safe.
  No `const enum` anywhere: it is not erasable syntax and breaks both Node type
  stripping and cross-file bundling.
- `src/git/executor.ts` — spawns git, streams stdout. No `vscode` import, so
  the whole git layer is testable in plain Node.
- `src/git/log.ts` — builds `git log` arguments and parses the output.
- `src/git/refs.ts` — branches, remotes, tags, stashes, HEAD state, and
  detection of an interrupted merge/rebase/cherry-pick/revert/bisect.
- `src/graph/layout.ts` — lane-allocation sweep producing columns, colours and
  edges.
- `test/layout.test.ts` (13 tests) — pure layout logic.
- `test/git.integration.test.ts` (13 tests) — runs real git against generated
  repositories containing Cyrillic, emoji, quotes, `$(...)`, pipes, multi-line
  bodies, merges, annotated and lightweight tags, detached HEAD, stashes, and a
  genuine merge conflict.

Phase 1 (session 2). **42/42 tests pass, `tsc --noEmit` clean, packaged and
installed.** Awaiting live verification by the user.

- `src/git/repository.ts` — repository discovery (enclosing repo + nested scan
  honouring `maxDepthOfRepoSearch`, skipping `node_modules` etc.). No `vscode`.
- `src/git/graphData.ts` — one call assembling commits, refs, stash rows and the
  Uncommitted Changes row. Handles empty repos and unborn HEAD (orphan branch).
- `src/repoManager.ts` — merges `vscode.git` API repos, the workspace scan and
  manually added repos (stored in `workspaceState`). Every Git-extension member is
  treated as possibly absent (#794, #863).
- `src/config.ts` — typed, validated reads of every setting.
- `src/view/protocol.ts` — discriminated-union messages both ways.
- `src/view/panel.ts` — single panel, CSP with nonce and no `unsafe-inline`,
  `retainContextWhenHidden`, serializer (restores after reload/restart),
  debounced file-watcher auto-refresh (deferred while hidden), stale-response
  guard via a load generation counter.
- `webview/main.ts`, `webview/menu.ts`, `webview/format.ts`,
  `webview/render/graph.ts`, `webview/render/table.ts`, `webview/style.css` —
  virtualised table (only visible rows + overscan in the DOM, graph SVG redrawn
  for the same window), sticky header (#132), ref labels with local/remote
  folding, date formats, load-more (auto and button), repo selector, remote
  toggle, own context menu (copy hash / subject / ref name), keyboard ↑/↓,
  scroll + repo persisted via `vscode.setState`.
- `src/extension.ts` — activation, commands (`view`, `viewForRepo`, `refresh`,
  `addGitRepository`, `removeGitRepository`), status bar item, serializer.
- Tests: `test/graphData.integration.test.ts` (7), `test/render.test.ts` (9).
- `.gitignore`, `.vscodeignore`, `@vscode/vsce` as a dev dependency.

### Not started

Commit details panel (click a commit → files changed, diff). Not in the Phase 1
list, but it is the first thing users will expect; proposed as the next step.

